# 11. INDEPENDENT INSTALLATION MODEL

This is a mandatory architectural requirement.

The same software repository must support many separate installations.

Every installation is a fully independent application instance.

Each instance must have its own:

- Database.
- Installation ID.
- Super Admin.
- Admin accounts.
- Client accounts.
- Encryption keys.
- Session secrets.
- Panel credentials.
- VPN records.
- Business settings.
- Audit records.
- Usage history.
- Domain.
- SSL certificate.
- Installed version.

There must be no central database dependency.

There must be no automatic cross-installation data synchronization.

Updating Installation A must never update Installation B.

Each owner controls upgrades separately.

Two separate Veylix installations should use separate 3X-UI panels for full operational isolation.

Sharing one external panel between separate installations creates shared-resource and client-identity conflict risks.

