# 12. INSTALLATION SYSTEM

## 12.1 One-Command Installer

The final product must support a documented single installation command for supported Linux servers.

The installer must:

1. Detect OS and CPU architecture.
2. Verify required permissions.
3. Check available RAM and disk.
4. Check existing installations.
5. Retrieve the selected release.
6. Verify checksums.
7. Create a dedicated service user.
8. Create protected application directories.
9. Generate unique installation secrets.
10. Initialize a fresh database.
11. Initialize installation identity.
12. Configure environment variables.
13. Validate embedded frontend assets.
14. Install the application binary.
15. Configure systemd.
16. Install or configure Caddy.
17. Collect domain information.
18. Verify DNS.
19. Obtain HTTPS certificates.
20. Configure firewall guidance.
21. Start the application.
22. Verify health.
23. Open first-time Super Admin setup.
24. Print installation summary.

The installer must never silently wipe an existing installation.

## 12.2 Domain and HTTPS

Support:

- Custom domain.
- DNS preflight.
- HTTPS.
- Automatic certificate renewal.
- Secure reverse proxy.
- Correct forwarded headers.
- Renewal monitoring.

## 12.3 Fresh Installation

Fresh installation must produce:

- Empty database.
- New installation identity.
- New encryption keys.
- New session secrets.
- First Super Admin setup.
- No previous users.
- No previous VPN assignments.
- No previous business history.
